        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "16fddb13-9259-3f5b-89c9-63ec49241960",
                "word": "incrédule",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "aba63be0-160b-48ee-aa79-d0539c32c5eb",
                        "entry_id": "16fddb13-9259-3f5b-89c9-63ec49241960",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "masculine",
                            "feminine"
                        ],
                        "form": "incrédules"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e1abcac9-a7c3-3fc6-aae3-c9bda13f6e99",
                        "entry_id": "16fddb13-9259-3f5b-89c9-63ec49241960",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui ne croit que difficilement, qu’on a peine à persuader ou à convaincre."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "38b7b4cc-5753-413f-a1d3-5007700bfe3e",
                                "sense_id": "e1abcac9-a7c3-3fc6-aae3-c9bda13f6e99",
                                "text": "Qu’importent à ce siècle incrédule nos merveilleuses légendes : …"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b4b289b9-fb44-4826-8aa1-a85d5ff3b9b4",
                                "sense_id": "e1abcac9-a7c3-3fc6-aae3-c9bda13f6e99",
                                "text": "Les raisonneurs les plus incrédules ne voulaient pas admettre une véritable métamorphose, opérée à l’aide ou sans l’aide de la peau enchantée d’un loup, qui, dans certains cas, était supposée coopérer à la transformation, et soutenaient que la lycanthropie n’était qu’une espèce de fatale maladie, une situation d’esprit mélancolique, auxquelles se joignaient des accès de folie, pendant lesquels le malade s’imaginait avoir commis les ravages dont il était accusé."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "be678521-b6dd-4ce5-8911-895a5f690ad7",
                                "sense_id": "e1abcac9-a7c3-3fc6-aae3-c9bda13f6e99",
                                "text": "Incrédule au merveilleux, Thucydide n'est pas moins ennemi de l'extraordinaire."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0b4048a5-e750-341c-9843-09e43edefb7e",
                        "entry_id": "16fddb13-9259-3f5b-89c9-63ec49241960",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui ne croit pas et ne veut pas croire aux mystères de la foi."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f31a8e14-5088-48a0-a376-b44ced26cbf4",
                        "source_entry_id": "16fddb13-9259-3f5b-89c9-63ec49241960",
                        "target_lang_word": "incredulous",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "incredulous",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4bcdbc1c-5379-31b6-86c0-3fde17f899cd",
                                        "entry_id": "bcf89979-6e3e-35d2-8f67-faa5199a093e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Skeptical, disbelieving, or unable to believe."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "164902da-f240-420d-8ac1-767d7147c0d5",
                                                "sense_id": "4bcdbc1c-5379-31b6-86c0-3fde17f899cd",
                                                "text": "Xodar listened in incredulous astonishment to my narration of the events which had transpired within the arena at the rites of Issus."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "29a418dc-3a6d-4d78-ac25-7d0eb864c5bd",
                                                "sense_id": "4bcdbc1c-5379-31b6-86c0-3fde17f899cd",
                                                "text": "In safe flats and dark restaurants, never the same one twice, we ate quiet meals, exchanged our goods and gazed upon each other with the incredulous contentment that passes between mountaineers when they are standing on the peak."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8c84ccaa-fef6-386c-ab7c-cd953f3e206b",
                                        "entry_id": "bcf89979-6e3e-35d2-8f67-faa5199a093e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Expressing or indicative of incredulity."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5ad32291-290a-4426-bcd3-f99d718a0133",
                                                "sense_id": "8c84ccaa-fef6-386c-ab7c-cd953f3e206b",
                                                "text": "Reactions at Sun's campus, an hour's drive from San Francisco, ranged from the fearful to the incredulous."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "40e0e487-d18a-4289-9674-65a4a4ff61e4",
                                                "sense_id": "8c84ccaa-fef6-386c-ab7c-cd953f3e206b",
                                                "text": "Then came a report over the radio from one of St. Los pilots. He was reporting seeing ships, and they weren't American. Worse still, they were close. Incredulous', Admiral Sprague demanded confirmation, and, circling in closer, the pilot radioed back: \"I can see pagoda masts. I see the biggest meatball flag on the biggest battleship I ever saw!\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d3b67990-99ee-3dad-8a0d-0a37c77ec9bd",
                                        "entry_id": "bcf89979-6e3e-35d2-8f67-faa5199a093e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Difficult to believe; incredible."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "nonstandard"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2e066c33-b813-4647-8b1f-445d5d5dd6bb",
                                                "sense_id": "d3b67990-99ee-3dad-8a0d-0a37c77ec9bd",
                                                "text": "1984, Supreme Court of Illinois, opinion in People v Terrell, 459 N.E.2d 1337, quoted in David C. Brody, James R. Acker, and Wayne A. Logan, Criminal Law, Jones & Bartlett Publishers (2001), →ISBN, page 564,\nFaced with these facts, we find it incredulous that [the] defendant had any intent other than the armed robbery of the service station."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "19a42854-da47-4e20-8c32-6b2056ba0c6b",
                                                "sense_id": "d3b67990-99ee-3dad-8a0d-0a37c77ec9bd",
                                                "text": "Why euery thing adheres togither, that no dramme of a scruple, no scruple of a scruple, no obstacle, no incredulous or vnsafe circumstance […]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9bfddda7-f90c-418f-84ed-916df3b29281",
                                                "sense_id": "d3b67990-99ee-3dad-8a0d-0a37c77ec9bd",
                                                "text": "Maybe David Ruben had some valid points about the ACLU on the national level from an historical perspective, although critcizing a non-gay organization for not loudly defending gay rights in 1952 seems a little incredulous."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "eaf40d92-0d88-47cc-83c4-d76ca34ced23",
                        "source_entry_id": "16fddb13-9259-3f5b-89c9-63ec49241960",
